    "answer": {
      "short": "Minimum $54$, lower quartile $64$, median $76$, upper quartile $82$, maximum $95$. Draw the box from $64$ to $82$, the median at $76$ and whiskers to $54$ and $95$.",
      "worked": "There are 30 ordered values. The 15th and 16th values are 75 and 77.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Median}&=\\frac{75+77}{2}\\\\\\text{Median}&=76\\end{align*}$$\n\nEach half contains 15 values. The lower quartile is the 8th value of the lower half, $64$. The upper quartile is the 8th value of the upper half, $82$. The minimum is $54$ and the maximum is $95$.\n\nDraw a labelled scale, a box from $64$ to $82$, a median line at $76$ and whiskers extending to $54$ and $95$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": [
        {
          "id": "p8-q4-solution-boxplot",
          "role": "solution",
          "format": "tikz",
          "code": "\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=2mm,y=1mm,line width=0.5pt,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont}]\n\\draw[->] (48,0)--(103,0);\n\\foreach \\x in {50,60,70,80,90,100}{\\draw (\\x,0)--(\\x,2);\\node[below,font=\\fontsize{8.5}{10}\\selectfont] at (\\x,0){\\x};}\n\\draw (54,10)--(64,10);\n\\draw (64,6) rectangle (82,14);\n\\draw (76,6)--(76,14);\n\\draw (82,10)--(95,10);\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
          "src": null,
          "widthMm": 115,
          "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
